# CODEOWNERS — ADR-002 § Branch protection and rulesets, item 7.
#
# Owner review is required for workflows, gate scripts, the required-check
# manifest, migrations, the API contracts, and the privacy/auth modules. The
# reason is concrete: a required-checks manifest edited in the same PR as the
# code it guards defeats the gate.
#
# NOTE: this file lists the owners. The RULESET that makes the review mandatory
# is applied by the repository owner after PR1 lands, because `ci-required` must
# exist before it can be a required check (ADR-002 item 9). Until that ruleset is
# applied, no ledger entry may reach VERIFIED on CI evidence alone (item 10).

# Default: the owner.
*                       @yegamble

# The gate itself.
/.github/               @yegamble
/.github/workflows/     @yegamble
/.github/required-checks.txt @yegamble
/.github/expected-ruleset.json @yegamble
/scripts/               @yegamble
/Makefile               @yegamble

# Contract sources. One owner per slice; other repositories consume them at a
# recorded commit SHA.
/api/                   @yegamble

# Append-only, and compiled into the release binary.
/migrations/            @yegamble
/sqlc.yaml              @yegamble
/store/queries/         @yegamble

# Privacy and authorization. ADR-002 names internal/auth*, internal/authz and
# internal/privacy explicitly.
/internal/authz/        @yegamble
/internal/auth/         @yegamble
/internal/privacy/      @yegamble
/internal/config/       @yegamble
